WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.200
There's a movement that is

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.300
upending shower routines
across the country.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.410
- There's a new trend in the beauty world.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.860
It's called the No Poo Method.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.190
- The secret could be not shampooing.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.480
Skip the shampoo.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.480
Your hair's better off without it.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.050
At least that's the slogan
for the No Poo Movement

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.420
that's got people claiming they haven't

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.080
used conventional shampoo in years.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.513
And their hair looks amazing.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.470
But is this just a fad?

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.210
What would really happen
if you didn't shampoo

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.693
your hair for an entire year?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.980
To find out, we asked
dermatologist Angela J. Lamb, MD,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.350
from Mount Sinai Hospital in New York.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.550
So what shampoos do mostly is they do

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.170
what's called saponification.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.305
So the actual shampoo comes along and

00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:50.341
wraps around oil and dirt,

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:54.033
and when you rinse, it kinda
comes out with the shampoo.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.810
You kinda rinse out both the
shampoo and the oil and dirt.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.150
But most conventional shampoos

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.040
are too good at what they do,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.220
stripping away too much oil
from your hair to the point

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.325
where you start producing
extra oil to compensate.

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:10.745
As a result, after the first
few days without using shampoo,

00:01:10.745 --> 00:01:14.717
your hair will look and feel
way more oily than normal,

00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:17.710
especially if you have straight hair.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.730
So for people that have
straighter-patterned hair,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.990
and like I said, what happens with that

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.520
patterned hair is the oils, the sebum,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.950
tend to progress down
the hair shaft faster,

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.333
so their hair is going to
feel oilier, dirtier sooner.

00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:31.283
After a month of no shampoo,

00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:34.560
that oil will have caught a
good amount of dead skin cells,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.660
dirt, and possibly even bacteria,

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.430
which could start to make your scalp itchy

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:42.300
and even smell kind of funky.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.560
I would say if you go
longer than about a month,

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.200
that you may see some,
again, what you would get

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.420
is sometimes odor, you
would get some trapping

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.970
of bacteria on your scalp.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.450
After six months to a year,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.830
all that gunk can clog
up your hair follicles,

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.560
which can prevent new hair
from growing and, over time,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.420
ultimately lead to hair
thinning or even hair loss.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.810
There's also a risk of
your scalp getting infected

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.903
from all the bacterial buildup.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.260
So the signs you want to
look for that would be

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.760
problematic that are
telling you you're not

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.710
washing your hair often
enough are scale, odor,

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:20.020
sometimes pimples that
lead...that are basically saying

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.020
you're getting an infection or bacteria.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.330
Those would be the signs that you would

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.360
know that you're not washing often enough.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.810
But here's the thing: rinsing your hair

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.300
with gentle cleaning
agents like baking soda

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.140
or even just plain
water is often enough to

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.048
prevent itching, hair loss, and infection.

00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:38.760
So how often should you be rinsing?

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.960
So to not wash at all, to use
no water, no cold washing,

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.040
no detergent, shampoo, I
think the cut off for how long

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.630
you can go really does depend
on your styling pattern.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.603
So many people can do
that for a couple of days,

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.140
some people can do it longer,
I would say two to four weeks,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.030
for example if your hair
is locked or if you have

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.330
any kind of prosthetic in your
hair like a weave or a braid,

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.990
you often can go a little
bit longer just because

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.310
of the way the hair is
kind of tied down and

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.970
not getting as disrupted.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.779
So if you would like to wash
your hair less frequently,

00:03:11.779 --> 00:03:14.720
try to go maybe I'd say about three days

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.590
to a week and see how you do.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.000
So you should still wash and rinse,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.680
but you don't have to
repeat every single day.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.443
Just try it out, and see how you do.

